{"author":{"id":"417295a7cc0952a9a38b67be3a894daed91f9069f7407e038d12a4f9b9a8451e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792344575,"nonce":"BtWwna3zrDmBIRDFSeXAfHFY4y4=","message":"Built (a4253bd): rayscript-vm and rayscript-cli.\n- Compiler: AST to 8-byte register instructions in two passes (which locals closures capture, which then live in cells; then emission). Module-level var and function are globals of their module, defined before anything runs so a script may call a function below it. Markup is lowered to `__el`, `__hole`, `__if`, `__for` and `__frag` calls with thunks for everything that can change (the view runtime that answers them is not written yet).\n- VM: fibers as data (stack, frames, handlers), run under a budget of polls (loop edges and calls) with an optional deadline; a poll also sees a cancel, collects, and fails the script on a refused allocation. try/catch with typed catches, closures with shared captures, switch with array, object and guard patterns, comprehensions, `await` on a fiber or a host promise, `spawn`, `yield`. Errors carry a trace with source positions.\n- Host module resolution, as the user asked: `import` asks the host. Natives are closures, so a module can hold state (a bridge to the Haxe side is natives sharing a handle). The host registers modules by path, or sets a ModuleResolver that answers for anything else with a value or the source of a script module (compiled and run once, its members imported; `import a.b.C`, `as`, `a.b.*`, and a member of a module by a longer path). Each script module has its own names; unload_module frees them. Dotted paths are also reachable by their package names (`haxe.Json`).\n- Standard library, in Haxe's own API and registered the way an embedder registers its own: Array, String, Map methods; Std, Math, StringTools, Lambda, Reflect, haxe.Json; new Array() and new Map().\n- `rayscript run|check|parse|dump`; `run` resolves imports from files beside the script.\n- Tests: 32 across fibers, collector, modules and the language; every language script is also run with a collection at every poll.\n- The heap is a stand-in with the same interface as rayscript-gc; the Immix port (WrenLift's collector, which is Immix only now) was started by a helper and stopped by a rate limit; its files are in crates/rayscript-gc, untracked, and it will be finished and swapped in.\n\nNext: the view runtime (signals, computed, effects, the element tree and the op stream), the host process and its protocol with the bridge to Haxe-side libraries (ashui, the editor's APIs) as remote modules, the Immix heap, native FFI, hot reload, the language support in RayDE.","files":null}]}